# Lumi post-training: active roadmap

Updated 2026-10-01. This is the current navigation/critical-path summary, **not a
new execution contract, gate, approval or replacement for frozen evidence**.
The old [v0.1 roadmap](posttraining-product-roadmap-v0.1.md) and numbered status
documents remain historical snapshots. Its opening September-5/v0.6 link and
older token-shortfall paragraphs are not the current task list.

## Where we actually are

| Original gate / component | Evidence-backed position |
| --- | --- |
| Gates 1–4: base pretraining and backup | Recorded complete: Lumi 4B, step 76,294, 80B pretraining tokens; original private S3 lineage remains bound. S3 availability was not refreshed in this review. |
| Gate 5: private research data selection/seal | Saved seal and independent verification pass; 309,643 train records and 19,557 validation records. |
| Gate 5: tokenization/encoded shards | Saved independent verification passes for nine train shards and one validation shard: 11,855,217 train supervised tokens, 939,293 validation supervised tokens. No new token selection is needed to close this existing work item. |
| Gate 5: checkpoint import | **Incomplete.** Tiny generated-input native import passed; actual full-size checkpoint import and independently verified, retained SFT package have not happened. |
| Gate 5: synthetic native watchdog | Verified in the one-shot AWS v0.3 attempt, with independent cleanup completion. This is not complete bootstrap or real checkpoint-import qualification. |
| Gate 6: GPU smoke/resume and SFT | Not started. A local/synthetic test count does not make this ready. |
| Gate 7: post-SFT quality/safety evaluation | Pending the SFT checkpoint. |
| Gate 8: serving/deployment | Pending required model, evaluation and production approvals. |

Latest verified result (2026-10-01): the [v0.3 watchdog outcome](../evidence/lumi-vm-watchdog-object-outcome-v0.3.json)
contains actual boot, ready and successful shutdown-observer receipts plus independently
observed STOP. Automatic cleanup verification failed; its original result is preserved.
Separate exact-resource verification and cleanup established that the new VM, volumes,
interface, security group and private report bucket are gone, without another launch
or report-object read. The unchanged report assessor then passed the narrow native
watchdog check. A teardown-metadata edge case was hardened locally and 37 guarded
tests passed, but the original cleanup error's exact transient cause was not captured.
No repeat watchdog run is required by this outcome. The existing full-bootstrap/host
admission and actual full-size import work below remain open; GPU/SFT has not started.

Fresh-host cloud-admission join (2026-10-01): the
[new outer setup join](../scripts/run_sft_vm_host_setup_v1.py) now connects
[fresh launch/volume and private-route checks](../scripts/prepare_sft_vm_host_connection_v2.py)
to the existing pinned SSH, seed/sender and guarded disk/setup delivery. The old
host checker alone did not prove the work volume was newly created without a
snapshot. The successor requires the provisioner's original dispatch record,
matching client token and launch/volume timestamps, exact root snapshot, blank
work snapshot and retained disks. It also requires an existing public-NAT-to-IGW
route for the private VM; failures prevent SSH/setup. No NAT is created or public
IP silently enabled. These are configuration checks, not live connectivity proof.

[Fresh-host local verification](../evidence/lumi-vm-fresh-host-local-verification-v0.1.json)
records 13 new and 365 combined passing tests with no skips or guard violations.
The joined test exercises the actual metadata validators, connection preparation,
seed/sender and setup delivery; only AWS responses and SSH/native execution are
doubled. The original deadlines and control budget are forwarded. Prior disk
sources, archive and evidence remain unchanged. Public AWS manuals were consulted;
no AWS API, SSH, VM, model/data, native disk or GPU operation ran.

**Provisioning is still incomplete:** these files consume a future authenticated
launch record; they do not create the host. Their launch-field projection is not
a runnable/approved request and does not bind early-stop UserData. Next is the
single resource-creation/initial-expiry/lifecycle controller. Actual route/quota/
price refresh, Linux admission and private retention/readback also remain open.
No live NAT availability or new work-volume provenance has been verified here.

