Historical setup return-contract correction (2026-10-01): the frozen storage/wheel path
returns a wrapper containing `storage_snapshot` and `setup`, but the previous
network bootstrap compared that wrapper with a flat setup receipt. Successful
setup would therefore be rejected before network transition. The previous tests
mocked this boundary with a flat result; their passing count did not cover this
actual return chain. No native full-bootstrap failure was needed to reproduce it.

The [corrected bootstrap](../scripts/run_sft_vm_network_bootstrap_v3.py) validates
the wrapper and unchanged storage floors, extracts `setup`, then still checks
the independently saved receipt. The [then-current delivery candidate](../scripts/run_sft_vm_setup_delivery_v2.py)
binds this correction through the versioned seed, sender, v0.4 control archive and
detached entry. Only the bootstrap archive member changed; the other 17 members
and all prior artifacts remain untouched. Do not use the historical v1 delivery
candidate below for a future full bootstrap.

[Correction verification](../evidence/lumi-vm-setup-return-contract-local-verification-v0.1.json)
records 71 focused and 258 combined passing local tests, no skips, no guard
violations and no ML imports. New tests join the actual bootstrap, wheel,
storage and offline setup functions and their receipt parsers; native effects
