“Supervised tokens” above are the tokens that contribute to training loss, not
all serialized input tokens. The saved train serialized total is 33,596,489;
validation is 2,295,902. The existing 10M research train-supervised-token floor
is exceeded. This does not establish model quality or production rights.

The research dataset is explicitly **non-production**. Nothing here promotes
sources, removes rights blockers, authorizes training, or claims a production
dataset seal. No dataset/model payload was reopened for this review.

## Why progress took too long

The delay is not SFT GPU runtime: GPU SFT has not begun. Much of the later work
was checkpoint-import infrastructure. The older bespoke write-meter/controller/
guardian route accumulated complexity; [v0.120](sft-execution-status-v0.120.md)
already selected a dedicated Linux VM and standard supervisor instead. That
engineering detour must not be described as time needed to select SFT tokens.

The necessary remaining import checks are real, but repeatedly treating small
validators and test-count increases as the next major milestone obscured the
distance to an actual run. The active overview also lagged behind the data
receipts. This document corrects the status and narrows the implementation
focus; it does not claim those unfinished checks have passed.

## Critical path; no new framework project

Implementation update (2026-09-28): the existing import handoff now has a
[completion adapter](../src/lumi/posttraining_vm_fullsize_completion_v1.py)
that runs the [existing SFT checksum consumer in a separate read-only unit](../scripts/verify_sft_vm_fullsize_package_v1.py),
reaps it, and fsyncs/preserves the complete output/evidence tree by a same-disk
rename. A joined tiny-package test exercises the actual checksum functions and
filesystem preservation. This is local integration, not a real 4B run. It does
not claim S3/off-host retention or permit instance termination.

The [acquisition child](../scripts/acquire_sft_vm_fullsize_inputs_v1.py) now calls
the existing exact-key transport/stager, and its
[root-parent wiring](../src/lumi/posttraining_vm_fullsize_acquisition_unit_v1.py)
connects acquisition to that same import/completion path. It uses acquisition-only
systemd credentials, an isolated writable acquisition directory (not a writable
alias of the release), a persistent one-shot dispatch marker and actual terminal/
empty-cgroup readback before moving the inputs into the handoff location.
The frozen handoff then stops the credential-bearing unit before import.
Failures preserve partial files and do not start the next phase or retry.

Local tests exercise the real frozen downloader/stager on tiny synthetic bodies
and the actual parent filesystem handoff; native systemd/SDK and completion
execution are doubled in these new tests. All 285 selected checks pass with no
network/payload guard violations. This is **not** native qualification of the
new acquisition entry or completion of Gate 5. The concrete host setup, pinned
Linux SDK/runtime qualification, authenticated release/storage/egress admission,
root credential-source teardown and approved off-host retention remain to be
finished. No route, model, tokenizer, dataset or frozen kernel changed.

