An important connection constraint is now explicit: AWS EICE TCP connections
last at most 3,600 seconds, whereas the existing root-parent deadline is 8,435
seconds. The configured connection cap is 120 seconds, for short commands.
The workflow must detach under systemd and collect durable status over later
read-only connections. It must not tie the entire import to one tunnel, resend
credentials after an ambiguous send or restart a started pass. The local
detached-parent protocol, controller-side SSH adapter and fixed root entry are
now implemented and locally joined as described below. The admitting native
bootstrap and installation/binding are **not yet complete**. Native
OS/storage/runtime/expiry/egress admission and retention are still open.
See the [AWS EICE documentation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/connect-with-ec2-instance-connect-endpoint.html).
No launch, SSH connection, live credential issuance, model download or GPU run
occurred in this preparation. The original proposal and source bundles remain
unchanged. Control-plane metadata checks alone are not native host admission.

Detached-parent update (2026-09-29): the
[new local protocol](../src/lumi/posttraining_vm_detached_parent_v1.py) provides
