credential workflow, separate-child cleanup through ExecStopPost, and aggregate
read-only status without re-delivery or restart. Parent normal exit also runs
cleanup (`RemainAfterExit=no`); credentials are not placed in argv or journals.
A real tiny FIFO joins the existing workflow in the local fixture, while Linux
identity, mounts, systemd and completion remain mocked. Fourteen new tests and
108 guarded regression tests pass with zero guard violations and no ML imports;
[the receipt](../evidence/lumi-vm-detached-parent-local-verification-v0.1.json)
also records the corrected development-test failures. The test entry is a
never-executed placeholder, not a runnable native controller. The subsequent
controller-side delivery update is recorded below. No live credentials, model reads, SSH, instance launch
or GPU were used. Frozen source files and earlier evidence are unchanged.

Short-SSH delivery update (2026-09-29): the
[controller adapter](../scripts/run_sft_vm_detached_delivery_v1.py) now constructs
fixed dispatch/submit/status/stop commands, rechecks the prepared SSH configuration
and host-key pins per connection, limits each exchange to 100 seconds and 4096
reply bytes, and carries credentials only through stdin. The issuer callback
waits for workflow completion and reaped children. Ambiguous dispatch/delivery
does not resend; it requests stop once and checks status. If stop cannot be
confirmed, the report says so, while the existing issuer still cleans its IAM
resources without claiming instantaneous session revocation.

The controller requires the already-running host's absolute deadline (at most
the proposal's 14,400 seconds remaining), reserving 120 seconds for cleanup.
It does not reset that host allowance or shorten the frozen parent limit of
8435 seconds by mistakenly treating it as the complete controller budget.
Thirteen new tests and 121 guarded regression tests pass, including real local
pipes and the existing issuer with synthetic IAM/STS; SSH processes and remote
responses are mocked. See the [receipt](../evidence/lumi-vm-detached-delivery-local-verification-v0.1.json).
This is **not native execution**: the subsequent root-entry update is below;
bootstrap/admission and actual deadline binding still must be supplied, followed
by retention/readback and bounded full-size-run approval. No live AWS, SSH, model
read, instance action or GPU was used for this update.

Root-entry update (2026-09-29): the fixed
[parent entry](../scripts/run_sft_vm_parent_entry_v1.py) now implements the
dispatch/submit/status/serve/stop interface expected by both the short-SSH
adapter and systemd parent. It verifies all nine pinned root-controller source
modules before loading any of them, without `lumi.__init__` or ML imports. It
requires the root-installed binding, matching machine/boot identity, unchanged
prepared descriptor and the existing host deadline. Source and host/no-swap
checks occur before credential input. Expiry blocks new work but leaves status
and stop available on the same bound boot.

Fifteen new local tests and 136 guarded regression tests pass with zero guard
violations. The actual pinned stdlib source closure loads locally; the entry's
dispatch/serve calls join the existing real tiny FIFO fixture. Native identity,
systemd, ownership/mount admission and completion remain mocked, not qualified.
See the [entry receipt](../evidence/lumi-vm-parent-entry-local-verification-v0.1.json).
No live binding was created and this entry is not installed on Linux. A trusted
