Exclusive creation, mode-0400 files, fsync, exact readback and failure preservation
are exercised locally. It never writes `binding.json` or `binding.sha256`, so
source installation does not authorize execution. The actual prepared archive
was independently unpacked and installed into a temporary directory with all
11 files/modes matched; native identity and root ownership were doubled.
The 160 guarded local tests include both entry versions (15 inherited v2 cases,
two new metadata cases and seven installer cases); zero guard violations or ML
imports. Portable unit tests use a synthetic descriptor, not private artifacts.
See the [install receipt](../evidence/lumi-vm-root-controller-install-local-verification-v0.1.json).

This closes **root-source packaging/install**, not the whole native bootstrap.
CPU/SDK runtime setup plus storage, egress and independent expiry checks still
