terminal, be stopped with an empty cgroup, and supply the expected aggregate
receipt before the next step starts. The CPU/SDK templates are reused as
transient exec units with explicit runtime limits and retained terminal state;
they are stopped after inspection. A failed or ambiguous step preserves evidence
and blocks the remaining sequence with no retry.

The caller must supply the original remaining setup deadline (at most 1800
seconds), with enough time for each complete next child and teardown. No live
