Network-boundary correction (2026-09-29): implementation review found that the
earlier roadmap conflated host packet quotas with a strict total inbound wire
cap. Host filtering processes packets that have already arrived; the tiny-VM
quota is not proof of the proposed full-size wire guarantee. See the
[boundary review and proposed correction](lumi-vm-network-budget-boundary-review-v0.1.md).
No numeric limits, frozen proposal, evidence or execution permission changed.
An explicit decision on that guarantee is needed before enabling the network
path. Exact payload/request limits remain intact, public dispatch stays closed,
and native expiry implementation remains pending. This was local/documentation
inspection only: no new test-count milestone, firewall action or cloud run.

