1. **One runnable CPU-import workflow.** Finish the authenticated root-parent/
   acquisition bootstrap around the existing standard systemd controls, exact
   S3 transport, staging and cold entry. Reuse the existing converter and SFT
   checksum consumer. Connect independent verification and durable package
   retention to that workflow. Bind the concrete host/runtime/storage and
   combined setup/transfer/import/verification/retention budget for approval.
   Acceptance: one concrete runnable workflow and an explicit bounded run
   proposal, not another disconnected validator or a new test-count target.
2. **One approved full-size CPU import.** Acquire only the existing pinned
   inputs, run once, preserve failed evidence without retry, independently check
   the package after worker termination, retain it and verify resource cleanup.
   Acceptance: the real package and verified lifecycle/retention evidence.
   No GPU rental is needed to complete this import.
3. **Gate 6.** After actual import, finish the SFT-specific launch binding,
   then the separately authorized GPU smoke/save/resume and bounded SFT.
   Do not run the legacy launcher unchanged: v0.120 records an authorization-
   before-CUDA ordering issue that still needs explicit closure.

Already completed work is not to be redone without evidence of a broken
binding: data selection, tokenization, the original model/tokenizer, and the
successful tiny native coordinator qualification. Do not add new data sources,
new token floors, a new converter/package format, generic native-write brokers,
extra pretraining, or production serving to this critical path. Preserve all
existing parser, provenance, rights, evaluation, resource and no-retry rules.
Any necessary contract change still needs its own explicit approval.

